{"audio": "1corinthians-11.opus", "voice": "Davis", "duration_ms": 222133, "sentences": [{"start_ms": 0, "end_ms": 2000, "text": "1 Corinthians, Chapter Eleven."}, {"start_ms": 2000, "end_ms": 6533, "text": "Be ye followers of me, even as I also am of Christ."}, {"start_ms": 6533, "end_ms": 13200, "text": "Now I praise you, brethren, that ye remember me in all things, and keep the ordinances, as I delivered them to you."}, {"start_ms": 13200, "end_ms": 21600, "text": "But I would have you know, that the head of every man is Christ; and the head of the woman is the man; and the head of Christ is God."}, {"start_ms": 21600, "end_ms": 26133, "text": "Every man praying or prophesying, having his head covered, dishonoureth his head."}, {"start_ms": 26133, "end_ms": 34400, "text": "But every woman that prayeth or prophesieth with her head uncovered dishonoureth her head: for that is even all one as if she were shaven."}, {"start_ms": 34400, "end_ms": 43067, "text": "For if the woman be not covered, let her also be shorn: but if it be a shame for a woman to be shorn or shaven, let her be covered."}, {"start_ms": 43067, "end_ms": 51333, "text": "For a man indeed ought not to cover his head, forasmuch as he is the image and glory of God: but the woman is the glory of the man."}, {"start_ms": 51333, "end_ms": 54400, "text": "For the man is not of the woman; but the woman of the man."}, {"start_ms": 54400, "end_ms": 59067, "text": "Neither was the man created for the woman; but the woman for the man."}, {"start_ms": 59067, "end_ms": 63867, "text": "For this cause ought the woman to have power on her head because of the angels."}, {"start_ms": 63867, "end_ms": 69600, "text": "Nevertheless neither is the man without the woman, neither the woman without the man, in the Lord."}, {"start_ms": 69600, "end_ms": 76267, "text": "For as the woman is of the man, even so is the man also by the woman; but all things of God."}, {"start_ms": 76267, "end_ms": 80667, "text": "Judge in yourselves: is it comely that a woman pray unto God uncovered?"}, {"start_ms": 80667, "end_ms": 86933, "text": "Doth not even nature itself teach you, that, if a man have long hair, it is a shame unto him?"}, {"start_ms": 86933, "end_ms": 92400, "text": "But if a woman have long hair, it is a glory to her: for her hair is given her for a covering."}, {"start_ms": 92400, "end_ms": 98000, "text": "But if any man seem to be contentious, we have no such custom, neither the churches of God."}, {"start_ms": 98000, "end_ms": 105600, "text": "Now in this that I declare unto you I praise you not, that ye come together not for the better, but for the worse."}, {"start_ms": 105600, "end_ms": 111867, "text": "For first of all, when ye come together in the church, I hear that there be divisions among you; and I partly believe it."}, {"start_ms": 111867, "end_ms": 118800, "text": "For there must be also heresies among you, that they which are approved may be made manifest among you."}, {"start_ms": 118800, "end_ms": 124133, "text": "When ye come together therefore into one place, this is not to eat the Lord's supper."}, {"start_ms": 124133, "end_ms": 131067, "text": "For in eating every one taketh before other his own supper: and one is hungry, and another is drunken."}, {"start_ms": 131067, "end_ms": 132000, "text": "What?"}, {"start_ms": 132000, "end_ms": 134400, "text": "have ye not houses to eat and to drink in?"}, {"start_ms": 134400, "end_ms": 138133, "text": "or despise ye the church of God, and shame them that have not?"}, {"start_ms": 138133, "end_ms": 139733, "text": "What shall I say to you?"}, {"start_ms": 139733, "end_ms": 141333, "text": "shall I praise you in this?"}, {"start_ms": 141333, "end_ms": 142267, "text": "I praise you not."}, {"start_ms": 142267, "end_ms": 158400, "text": "For I have received of the Lord that which also I delivered unto you, That the Lord Jesus the same night in which he was betrayed took bread: And when he had given thanks, he brake it, and said, Take, eat: this is my body, which is broken for you: this do in remembrance of me."}, {"start_ms": 158400, "end_ms": 170267, "text": "After the same manner also he took the cup, when he had supped, saying, This cup is the new testament in my blood: this do ye, as oft as ye drink it, in remembrance of me."}, {"start_ms": 170267, "end_ms": 175867, "text": "For as often as ye eat this bread, and drink this cup, ye do shew the Lord's death till he come."}, {"start_ms": 175867, "end_ms": 183333, "text": "Wherefore whosoever shall eat this bread, and drink this cup of the Lord, unworthily, shall be guilty of the body and blood of the Lord."}, {"start_ms": 183333, "end_ms": 188400, "text": "But let a man examine himself, and so let him eat of that bread, and drink of that cup."}, {"start_ms": 188400, "end_ms": 194800, "text": "For he that eateth and drinketh unworthily, eateth and drinketh damnation to himself, not discerning the Lord's body."}, {"start_ms": 194800, "end_ms": 199200, "text": "For this cause many are weak and sickly among you, and many sleep."}, {"start_ms": 199200, "end_ms": 202800, "text": "For if we would judge ourselves, we should not be judged."}, {"start_ms": 202800, "end_ms": 209467, "text": "But when we are judged, we are chastened of the Lord, that we should not be condemned with the world."}, {"start_ms": 209467, "end_ms": 214133, "text": "Wherefore, my brethren, when ye come together to eat, tarry one for another."}, {"start_ms": 214133, "end_ms": 219733, "text": "And if any man hunger, let him eat at home; that ye come not together unto condemnation."}, {"start_ms": 219733, "end_ms": 222133, "text": "And the rest will I set in order when I come."}], "words": [{"t": "1", "s": 0, "e": 444, "si": 0}, {"t": "Corinthians,", "s": 444, "e": 1091, "si": 0}, {"t": "Chapter", "s": 1232, "e": 1556, "si": 0}, {"t": "Eleven.", "s": 1596, "e": 1899, "si": 0}, {"t": "Be", "s": 2722, "e": 2802, "si": 1}, {"t": "ye", "s": 2923, "e": 2983, "si": 1}, {"t": "foll